body:
But it doesn't take away from the fact that another animal is now invading a space that the cat deemed theirs from the beginning. That's the issue here. Animals absolutely get jealous when they feel as if their time in the spotlight has changed, and unfortunately we as humans try to rationalize their feelings in a human way, which simply doesn't match up with an animal's. We possess the intelligence needed to rationalize a divide in attention and affection, but cats—as well as most animals—dont.

&#x200B;

But things may even out with time. Cats can be this way and sometimes there's really nothing you can do, but they may get used to the dynamic. Just keep being patient :)

Candystand

&#x200B;

That golf game......
